@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the lifecycle of a proveo-rendered sbx Kit and its deterministic sandbox
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox_stale_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/run.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/stop_signal_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/clone_carry_test.go
'
' ── A KEPT SANDBOX MUST NOT SILENTLY OVERRIDE THIS RUN (2026-09-27) ─────────
' Re-attach passes the name only, so a kept sandbox runs with the Kit, image
' and env it was CREATED with. Measured: a hermes run with the host-chrome add-on
' ticked re-attached to a sandbox kept from an earlier run; PID 1 and the agent
' still carried the earlier PROVEO_EGRESS_SESSION_ID, PROVEO_HOST_CDP_PORT never
' arrived, and the agent drove the in-sandbox headless Chromium. sbx's help says
' -e "takes effect on a re-attach too"; proveo never passes it there.
' The fix is a RECEIPT written at creation (os.UserCacheDir()/proveo/
' sbx-sandboxes/<name>.json): image + local image ID, Kit digest, clone, mounts,
' and a digest per env var, with the session ID normalised to <sid> (two dry
' runs then compare identical). On reuse:
'   same receipt            → re-attach, as before
'   changed, headed         → ask. Yes runs the three steps for every harness:
'     carry clone and agent state home, sbx rm --force, create the same name.
'     The session does not persist. Host proveo files stay.
'     No keeps it. A running one is re-attached and the new settings do not apply.
'     A stopped one stays. This run stops, and the next proveo run asks again.
'   changed, not headed, stopped → the same three steps, no question
'   changed, not headed, running → warn. The session stays. The new settings do not apply.
' A headed yes removes a running sandbox except an OpenCode engine with active,
' unpublished, or unattested state. That engine must be recovered before replacement.
' A screen that fails to open counts as no, so a stopped sandbox is not removed.
'
' ── A FORWARDED STOP TEARS DOWN LIKE A NORMAL EXIT AND EXITS 128+sig ────────
' DECIDED 2026-10-17, twice. Teardown: the user chose "Stop runs normal
' teardown". Exit status: the user chose "Exit 128+sig, 'stopped'
' (Recommended)". MEASURED (internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go Run):
'   forwardStop returns (ctx, stop, cancel, signalled func() syscall.Signal);
'     signalled is 0 when proveo cancelled the run itself (Ctrl+C remove).
'   stopOutcome(runErr, sig, forced) returns (teardown, result). For sig != 0
'     and not forced: teardown nil, result backend.Stopped{sig}. Otherwise both
'     are runErr. The signal is read ONCE, after the retry block.
'   Run prints "stopped by SIGTERM — ending as on a normal exit" (or SIGHUP).
'     Teardown takes the SUCCESS branch: clone edits and commits lifted, state
'     saved, `sbx rm`; an OpenCode engine is retained.
'   Run returns Stopped, and cmd/proveo main's exitCode maps it to 128+signal:
'     143 for SIGTERM, 129 for SIGHUP (_spec/internal/backend/exit-code.puml).
'     The transcript reads "outcome: stopped by SIGTERM".
'   No template-reload retry after a stop: Run checks signalled() == 0 before
'     sbx.ReloadTemplate and again before the retry run. ReloadTemplate takes
'     no context, so a stop during the reload waits for it to finish.
'   After the first signal, later SIGTERM/SIGHUP are swallowed until teardown
'     ends — by design: the scheduler SIGTERMs, then kill-session (SIGHUP)
'     after termGrace = 1 min (internal/schedule/runner.go:37), and a longer
'     teardown must not be cut short. Only SIGKILL interrupts a hung teardown.
' [Inference] A stop that lands while an already-failed run's sbx client is
' still exiting reads as a stop: normal teardown, exit 143, and the sandbox
' holding the failure evidence is removed. The sbx client's own exit after the
' agent ends bounds that window.
' HISTORY: before 2026-10-17 a stop read as a failed run ("kept for
' diagnosis", no `sbx rm`). An earlier revision that day made a stop exit 0;
' the exit-status decision replaced it. Pinned by
' TestAForwardedStopTearsDownLikeANormalExitAndReportsTheSignal (including the
' Ctrl+C remove path, sig 0 + forced, and "a signal after the operator chose
' remove"), TestACancelWithoutASignalIsNotAStop and
' TestHangupCancelsTheRunInsteadOfKillingProveo (stop_signal_test.go).
' The kept-for-diagnosis hint names `sbx exec -it <name> bash` (MEASURED),
' matching https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/sbx/exec/.
'
' ── WORK STRANDED IN THE SANDBOX KEEPS THE SANDBOX (2026-10-17) ─────────────
' MEASURED: PreserveClone and TeardownClone return an error while work remains
' only in the sandbox — snapshot failed ("uncommitted work is still only in
' <name>") or carry failed ("the agent's branches are still only in <name>").
' Normal-exit and stop teardown then skip `sbx rm`, print "<err> — <name> kept;
' `sbx rm --force <name>` deletes it once the work is home", keep home access
' and print the IDE attach. retireSandbox (the stale-sandbox upgrade,
' launch_receipt.go) returns the same error before SaveState and `rm`. The
' forced Ctrl+C remove still deletes: its dialog says "Uncommitted changes can
' be permanently lost" (internal/choiceui/sandbox_close.go). Detail:
' _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml.
title sbx Kit lifecycle — create with a Kit, reuse by name, keep failures and stranded work, remove success and stops

state "resolve full RunConfig\n+ render Kit spec.yaml" as RESOLVE
state "sandbox name exists?" as EXISTS <<choice>>
state "fresh launch config\nname + Kit + image + env + agent\n+ mounts/clone/ports/limits" as CREATE
state "receipt matches?" as DRIFT <<choice>>
state "carry clone + state home\nsbx rm --force" as RETIRE
state "reattach launch config\nname + trailing agent args ONLY" as REUSE
state "sbx run" as RUN
state "sandbox exists after error?" as CREATED <<choice>>
state "reload image template\nretry once with FULL create config" as RETRY
state "agent/session running" as LIVE
state "child result" as RESULT <<choice>>
state "preserve clone + sync state\nusing the retained FULL config" as PRESERVE
state "kept for diagnosis" as KEPT
state "kept: work still only\nin the sandbox" as STRANDED
state "sbx rm --force" as REMOVE
state "removed" as REMOVED
state "removal warning\nsandbox remains stale" as STALE
state "stopped sandbox kept\nnext run asks again" as ASKAGAIN
state "launch failed\nno sandbox to retain" as FAILED

[*] --> RESOLVE
RESOLVE --> EXISTS : WriteKit is per run;\nsecret values are never in it
EXISTS --> CREATE : no
EXISTS --> DRIFT : yes
DRIFT --> REUSE : receipt matches,\nor running and headed no,\nor running and not headed
DRIFT --> RETIRE : changed and headed yes,\nor stopped and not headed
DRIFT --> ASKAGAIN : stopped and headed no
RETIRE --> CREATE : clone carried home
RETIRE --> STRANDED : clone not carried\n(retireSandbox errors; this run stops)
CREATE --> RUN
REUSE --> RUN
RUN --> LIVE : agent session opens
RUN --> CREATED : command error before session
CREATED --> RETRY : no, and no stop signalled
RETRY --> RUN : template reload succeeded\nand still no stop
RETRY --> FAILED : reload or retry failed
RETRY --> PRESERVE : a stop signalled during the reload\n(no retry run; exits 128+sig)
CREATED --> PRESERVE : yes, or a stop signalled
LIVE --> RESULT : sbx child exits
RESULT --> PRESERVE : exit != 0
RESULT --> PRESERVE : exit == 0
RESULT --> PRESERVE : SIGTERM/SIGHUP forwarded\n(teardown nil, result Stopped)
PRESERVE --> KEPT : run failed
PRESERVE --> STRANDED : snapshot or carry failed\n(not the Ctrl+C remove path)
PRESERVE --> REMOVE : run succeeded, or stopped by a signal;\nproveo exits 0, or 128+sig for a stop
STRANDED --> REMOVE : operator, once the work is home
STRANDED --> [*]
REMOVE --> REMOVED : success or already absent
REMOVE --> STALE : other error; warn
KEPT --> REUSE : next proveo run,\nsame target + workspace
KEPT --> REMOVE : operator cleanup
STALE --> REUSE : next proveo run
ASKAGAIN --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
REMOVED --> [*]

note right of CREATE
  **Creation-only fields travel once.**
  sbx accepts the Kit, template, environment,
  agent, workspace, clone, ports and limits only
  while creating the named sandbox.
end note

note right of REUSE
  **The stored spec owns a reused sandbox.**
  Passing ""--kit"" here is rejected before the
  agent starts: ""--kit can only be used when
  creating a new sandbox"".

  The same applies to every other creation-only
  field. The supported shape is:
  ""sbx run --name <existing> [-- AGENT_ARGS…]"".
end note

note bottom of PRESERVE
  **Launch config and lifecycle metadata differ.**
  Reattach strips fields from the argv, not from
  proveo's retained full config. Clone recovery
  still needs the workspace path; state sync still
  needs the host state-home environment.
end note

note bottom of KEPT
  **Failure retains evidence deliberately.**
  The next run reuses the VM by its fixed name;
  the hint names ""sbx exec -it <name> bash"" and
  ""sbx rm --force <name>"". A forwarded stop is
  not a failure since 2026-10-17.
end note

note bottom of STRANDED
  **Work only in the sandbox keeps it.** A
  failed snapshot or carry skips ""sbx rm"" and
  says so; the forced Ctrl+C remove still
  deletes, as its dialog warns.
end note

note bottom of REMOVE
  **Success is disposable.** After clone output and
  state are copied home, proveo removes the sandbox.
  A removal failure is warning-only but leaves a
  stale name that follows the reuse branch next run.
end note
@enduml
